    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cloudina-hartmannae-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cloudina hartmannae wall-normal Turing lamella at 2.397 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Re-run of the 2.397 µm wall-normal Schnakenberg model (a=0.0642, b=0.9915, Dv/Du=8.65, seed 3149, Nama Group 549 Ma). Noise-seeded integration on the 19.176 µm layer selects 8 lamellae at 2.397 µm. Real-eigenvalue growth rates match the analytical dispersion with Pearson r=0.99997 and RMSE=0.0312. Scaling both diffusivities by s moves the peak wavelength monotonically (sweep r=0.9999). Equal diffusion gives σmax=-0.124. Removing u^2 v drops the activator standard deviation from 0.164 to ~1e-14. Species-card foreground fraction 0.364 versus 0.635 on the Corumbá fossil photograph. GIF last-frame CV similarity against the species card is 91.5 (12 frames, 640×480). The KS test against N(2.75 µm, 1.125 µm) rejects (statistic 0.623, p=0.0016): the simulator locks to one wavelength inside the Yang band and does not sample the whole 0.5–5 µm range. Spacing standard deviation is 0 because the domain is exactly eight critical wavelengths. Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 87.4, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/cloudina_hartmannae_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cloudina-hartmannae-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 379283 B, 1344×984 px, artifact_sha256 bb3134888de8b71deb15f05bdbb0d2af68dad34b28b237c32208765ed9a18d64 (sha256 bb3134888de8b71deb15f05bdbb0d2af68dad34b28b237c32208765ed9a18d64), spec_fingerprint aed8c0ba57f9ef79f97072aa88a12b01ec7259b22f96b35a3a9a2a503fa4efe9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: aed8c0ba57f9ef79f97072aa88a12b01ec7259b22f96b35a3a9a2a503fa4efe9; artifact_sha256: bb3134888de8b71deb15f05bdbb0d2af68dad34b28b237c32208765ed9a18d64; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cloudina_hartmannae_turing_wavelength_s0/cloudina_corumba_cc_by_2.jpg=f20328a5dcb570d1..., datasets/cloudina_hartmannae_turing_wavelength_s0/cloudina_hartmannae_specimen.jpg=cbe0233dbf275f4e..., datasets/cloudina_hartmannae_turing_wavelength_s0/cloudina_hartmannae_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=dcd1cbc35eecb656...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-cloudina-hartmannae-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yang et al. 2020: Namibian Cloudina organic lamellae 0.5–5 µm, up to eight per wall layer | Grant 1990: shell layers 8–50 µm | Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Penny et al. 2014: Omkyk ash 547.32 ± 0.31 Ma; slot age remains 549 Ma; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian and diffusivities with lambda_c fixed at 2.397 µm and a small positive discriminant | Noise-seeded nonlinear stack, equal-diffusion control, autocatalysis ablation, diffusivity sweep | Segmentation of the species card and the CC BY 2.0 Corumbá photograph; transfer_boundary: Applying a reaction-diffusion lamella wavelength to Cloudina is a morphospace hypothesis | Grant's cnidarian-grade reading and Yang's annelid-grade reading are both left open; does_not_claim: That Cloudina had ocelli or a measured pigment stripe at 2.397 µm | That the species card or the Corumbá slab is a Nama Group lamella SEM | That the Wikimedia life restoration is a fossil photograph | That slot 1252 parameters were copied." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Closed from Pass 1: diffusivity sweep (r=0.9999, monotone), equal-diffusion and ablation controls, card-versus-Corumbá segmentation, and dispersion r/RMSE with the KS rejection reported as a rejection.",
        "remediation needed: Still open: a Nama Group thin-section of C. hartmannae lamellae would replace the species-card CV target and the band-midpoint comparison.",
        "remediation needed: Still open: lean binary was not available, and no second assessor scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: Still open: spacing standard deviation is 0 on a domain of exactly eight critical wavelengths; an incommensurate domain would separate mode selection from grid locking." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.81e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cloudina-hartmannae-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cloudina hartmannae wall-normal Turing lamella at 2.397 µm (Pass 2) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Multiplying both diffusivities by s in {0.64, 0.81, 1, 1.21, 1.44, 1.69, 1.96} moves the numerical peak wavelength with the analytical curve λ=2.397√s. Sweep Pearson r=0.9999 and the sequence is monotone. That is the expressivity check Pass 1 asked for. Equal diffusion, a separate axis, shuts the instability off." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cloudina-hartmannae-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cloudina-hartmannae-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

